"view.synastry.help.title"                  = "Help";
"view.synastry.help.close"                  = "Close";
"view.synastry.help.input"                  = "This screen lets you calculate 6 different synastry techniques: Compare, Composite, Combine (Davison), Aspect Comparison, Midpoint Comparison and Declination Comparison.\n\nSearch for a chart by (part of) its name and click a result to add it to the selection. Compare, Aspect Comparison, Midpoint Comparison and Declination Comparison require exactly two selected charts. Composite and Combine work with two or more charts.\n\nOnce you have selected the charts you need, click one of the buttons below to calculate the corresponding technique.";
"view.synastry.help.compare"                = "Here you see the chart of one of the two selected charts, with the positions of the other chart plotted in the outer ring.\n\nUse the swap button to switch which chart forms the inner wheel and which forms the outer ring. You can display the chart in black-and-white or color, with or without aspects, and you can export the drawing using the icons above it.";
"view.synastry.help.composite"              = "You can choose between two forms of the composite: a calculation using midpoints only, including for the cusps, or a calculation using a reference location.\n\nKeep in mind that a composite chart can contain configurations that are astronomically impossible - for example, Sun opposite Venus.";
"view.synastry.help.combine"                = "Here you have four options: Simplified, Original, Reference location and Spherical midpoint.\n\nSimplified uses the arithmetic mean of the birth times and locations. Original solves the time so the resulting chart's Midheaven matches the mean of the natal Midheavens. Reference location keeps the mean time but lets you choose the location. Spherical midpoint uses the true geographic midpoint between the locations.";
"view.synastry.help.aspectcomparison"       = "Here you see the aspects between the factors of both charts. There are two tables, one for each chart. The aspects in both tables are the same but grouped differently.\n\nYou can export the results to PDF.";
"view.synastry.help.midpointcomparison"     = "This screen shows the midpoints graphically and as a table, separately for both charts: each chart's own factor-pair midpoints, tested against the other chart's factors as occupants.\n\nUse the 360/90/45 dial selector to change how strict the matches are. You can export the results to PDF.";
"view.synastry.help.declinationcomparison"  = "Here you see, for both charts, a table with parallels and contra-parallels and the orb. The content of both tables is the same but ordered differently.\n\nYou can export the results to PDF.";
